«
@@ ============================================================
@@ Exmnf — examine a function over an interval: draw f over X,
@@ with the smallest and largest values found by ΔRf.
@@
@@ Input:  'f(x)' X, as for ΔRf.
@@ Output: the drawing, and on the stack the result of ΔRf.
@@ The curve uses 161 points; the dashed lines are the bounds
@@ given by ΔRf. A bound that does not touch the curve, or a peak
@@ of the curve beyond a line, shows an extremum that ΔRf missed.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@ ============================================================

  → fx xv
  «
    'fx' Rcl xv ⓁΔRf
    @ Bounds of X as numbers, and its unit
    1 xv
    If xv TypeName "unit" == Then Drop Drop 1 xv →Unit xv UVal End
    Dup TypeName
    → rsl un iv tn
    «
      Case
        tn "range" == Then iv Explode End
        tn "drange" == Then iv Explode → cv dv « cv dv - cv dv + » End
        tn "prange" == Then
          iv Explode → cv pv « cv Abs pv * 100 / → dv « cv dv - cv dv + » »
        End
        iv iv
      End
      @ Bounds of the result as numbers, and its unit
      1 rsl
      If rsl TypeName "unit" == Then Drop Drop 1 rsl →Unit rsl UVal End
      Dup TypeName
      → lo hi uf rv rt
      «
        If rt "range" == Then rv Explode Else rv Explode → cv dv « cv dv - cv dv + » End
        → rlo rhi
        «
          @ 161 values of f, as numbers in the unit of the result
          0 160 For kk
            { x 0 } 2 lo hi lo - kk * 160 / + un * Put
            'fx' Rcl Swap Where →Num
            If uf TypeName "unit" == Then uf Convert UVal End
          Next
          161 →List
          → ys
          «
            @ Vertical scale: the curve and the bounds, with a margin
            ys Sort Dup 1 Get rlo Min Swap Dup Size Get rhi Max
            → ya yb
            «
              If yb ya == Then ya 1 - 'ya' Store yb 1 + 'yb' Store End
              FromLCD Size Drop B→R
              → wd
              «
                ClearLCD
                "Exmnf: " 'fx' Rcl →Str + " over X" +
                If Dup Size 46 > Then 1 45 Sub "…" + End
                { #0d #2d 0 true false } DrawText
                @ Plot area: columns 8 to wd-12, rows 34 to 150
                @ Frame, closed at both ends of X
                { #8d #34d } { #8d #150d } DrawLine
                { #8d #150d } wd 12 - R→B #150d 2 →List DrawLine
                wd 12 - R→B #34d 2 →List wd 12 - R→B #150d 2 →List DrawLine
                @ The curve
                0 160 For kk
                  8 wd 20 - kk * 160 / + 0 RND R→B
                  150 116 ys kk 1 + Get ya - * yb ya - / - 0 RND R→B
                  2 →List
                  If kk 0 > Then Dup Rot Swap DrawLine End
                Next
                Drop
                @ Local extrema of the curve: ▲ above a point higher than its two
                @ neighbours, ▼ below a point lower than them (ties go to the left one)
                2 160 For kk
                  ys kk 1 - Get ys kk Get ys kk 1 + Get
                  → pa pv pc
                  «
                    8 wd 20 - kk 1 - * 160 / + 0 RND 4 -
                    150 116 pv ya - * yb ya - / - 0 RND
                    → mx my
                    «
                      If pv pa > pv pc ≥ And Then
                        "▲" mx R→B my 15 - 34 Max R→B 2 →List 0 true false 3 →List + DrawText
                      End
                      If pv pa < pv pc ≤ And Then
                        "▼" mx R→B my 2 + 137 Min R→B 2 →List 0 true false 3 →List + DrawText
                      End
                    »
                  »
                Next
                @ The bounds found by ΔRf, dashed
                rlo rhi 2 →List
                1 2 For jj
                  Dup jj Get
                  150 116 Rot ya - * yb ya - / - 0 RND R→B
                  → py
                  «
                    8 wd 12 - For cx
                      cx R→B py 2 →List cx 4 + R→B py 2 →List DrawLine
                    8 Step
                  »
                Next
                Drop
                @ The numbers
                "x: " lo un * →Str + " … " + hi un * →Str + "   [▲: max ; ▼: min]" +
                { #0d #160d 0 true false } DrawText
                "min = " rlo uf * →Str + { #0d #180d 0 true false } DrawText
                "max = " rhi uf * →Str + { #0d #200d 0 true false } DrawText
                rsl
              »
            »
          »
        »
      »
    »
  »
»
